# Local-only (no Cursor Cloud)

**Do not use Cursor Cloud Agents** for Sync2Dine work. Always work on this Windows machine against the local repos:

- `C:\Users\dolab\Downloads\sync2dine-frontend`
- `C:\Users\dolab\Downloads\sync2dine-backend`

## Why

Cloud agents cannot reach the VPS (`ssh vps` / `C:\Users\dolab\.ssh\id_ed25519`), so they cannot restart the live API or run `push-live-local.sh`. Cloud sessions leave GitHub and production out of sync with what the user expects.

## Required workflow

1. Edit and verify **locally**.
2. Commit on `master` (or merge into `master`).
3. `git push origin master` (HTTPS + Credential Manager).
4. Ship live from this PC: `bash scripts/push-live-local.sh` (SPA + API via `ssh vps`).
5. Prove live: `curl https://app.sync2dine.io/health` and `/api/vapi/health`.

## Forbidden

- Starting or continuing Sync2Dine tasks in Cursor Cloud Agents
- Assuming a cloud push updated production (it does not without local VPS deploy)
- Asking the user to authorize a different cloud SSH key when local `ssh vps` already works
